  "result": "Here's a draft. I haven't added it to `README.md` yet.\n\n```markdown\n## Carriers\n\nEach carrier has its own module in `shop/carriers/`, such as `acme.py` or `maple.py`.\nA module defines a `BASE_RATE` in cents, a per-weight charge, a `ZONES` table of\nmultipliers (`local`, `regional`, `national`) and a weight limit. Its carrier class\nquotes `(BASE_RATE + per-weight charge \u00d7 weight) \u00d7 zone factor` and raises\n`ValueError` if the weight is out of range.\n\nAll carriers take weight in kilograms except **Maple**, which takes grams\n(`PER_GRAMS`, up to `MAX_GRAMS = 30000`). Convert weights before asking Maple for a quote.\n```\n\nThat's about 75 words. I checked it against the code: all 20 carrier modules define `BASE_RATE`, 19 of them use kg, and `maple.py` is the only one that uses grams. Do you want me to add it to `README.md`?",
